  today. `lib/ui/output.sh`'s own comment points at
  `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §8 for "which fatal helper survives" — but
  that document is `beta`-scoped (§12), so this specific question has
  **no `variant-f-j`-scoped answer on record**. This is real, minor,
  P3-level cleanup debt, not a correctness bug (both behave
  identically today).
- I did not re-run the "63 UI-emitting functions × every `$(...)`
  call site" repo-wide cross-reference this session (the two known
  historical offenders are fixed, per §2, but a full re-sweep is cheap
  and was out of scope for a read-only review — see §14, item 2, for
  why this is worth doing *before*, not during, the next stage).

