## 6. Remote Node lifecycle — target model, confirmed/refuted

Task's proposed model, checked line-by-line against
`lib/panel/node/api.sh` and `lib/panel/node/install.sh`:

```
install
  ├── identity lookup            ✅ REAL — GET /api/nodes + name filter
  │
  ├── NOT FOUND
  │      └── CREATE               ✅ REAL — POST with rollback of
  │                                    profile+node on downstream failure
  │
  └── FOUND
         │
         ├── healthy + desired state matches
         │       └── NO-OP        ⚠️ PARTIAL — reuses the found Node's
         │                            uuid and skips re-creating it, but
         │                            there is no drift check at all: a
         │                            changed NODE_ADDR/IP on a re-run is
         │                            silently NOT reapplied to the
         │                            existing Node object. "NO-OP" is
         │                            accidentally correct only because
         │                            nothing is compared, not because a
         │                            match was confirmed.
         │
         ├── healthy + drift
         │       └── RECONCILE     ❌ DOES NOT EXIST — no code path
         │                            compares any field of an existing
         │                            Node/Host against desired values
         │
         └── unhealthy / incomplete
                 └── REPAIR/RECONCILE  ❌ DOES NOT EXIST — no health
                                          read exists for Remote Node at
                                          all (only `panel_node_wait_
                                          connected()`'s one-shot
                                          isConnected poll, run only
                                          immediately after a fresh
                                          registration, never on a
                                          "found existing" path)

explicit reinstall
  └── reinstall runtime while preserving node identity
        ❌ DOES NOT EXIST as a distinct operation. The remote-host
        deployment half (file copy + `docker compose up -d`) always
        re-executes unconditionally on every invocation, regardless of
        whether Panel-side objects already existed — this is not a
        "reinstall" abstraction, it's the simple absence of a
        Panel-side/remote-host state check being kept in sync. Recorded
        as a documentation/code inconsistency: the operator-facing
        warning text ("Повторный запуск создаст новую ноду/хост... —
        операция не идемпотентна") is now FALSE for the Panel-API half
        (Node/Host ARE reused) but TRUE for the remote-host half
        (compose/files ARE unconditionally rewritten and restarted) —
        the single warning conflates two different actual behaviors.
```

**Verdict on the proposed model**: partially real. CREATE (with
identity + rollback) is solid and already better than what
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`/`docs/CONTRACTS.md` describe for `beta`.
RECONCILE/REPAIR/REINSTALL are correctly identified as *targets*, not
current behavior — the code's own comment
(`api.sh:222-225`) says so explicitly. I am not adopting the model as
"the" target architecture just because it was proposed; I'm confirming
the CREATE slice is real and the rest is, so far, only named
vocabulary with zero implementation — same conclusion
`CORE_RUNTIME_CONTRACTS.md` §7/§14 already reached, independently
re-confirmed this session.

**Identity ownership**: settled — `Nodes.name` is the only identity
key; address/SSH/credentials/hostname are confirmed NOT part of it.

