## 14. Final synthesis

### Architecture verdict

The target architecture in `docs/CORE_RUNTIME_CONTRACTS.md` is, to the
extent it has been implemented at all, **confirmed by code and
tests** — not just asserted. What's built (Topology, Deployment
resolution, two Core adapters, RuntimeComponent inventory, Remote Node
CREATE-with-rollback) works, is tested, and is MODE-blind exactly as
designed. What's *not* built (Reconciler, general health/observed
state, RECONCILE/REPAIR/REINSTALL for anything, a real Capability→
Adapter code seam) is **correctly and honestly labeled as not built**
in the existing docs — I found no case this session where the
documentation overclaims what exists in `variant-f-j` itself. The only
overclaiming problem is the **other**, `beta`-scoped documents being
read as if they describe this branch — a documentation-hygiene issue,
not an architecture-honesty issue.

